+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"Done. The versioned document store is implemented, tested, and verified.\n\n**Files**\n- `src/index.ts:1` — full implementation: `DocumentStore` class, plus `createDocumentStore()` factory and a default export\n- `tests/document-store.test.ts:1` — 35 tests covering CRUD, history, branching, and merge semantics\n\n**Design**\n- **Storage** — each branch maps document ids to `{ alive, versions[] }`; every `create`/`update` appends a deep-cloned version with a unique id (`v1`, `v2`, …) and `Date.now()` timestamp. Branching deep-copies document state so branches are fully isolated.\n- **Common ancestor** — for each document, the merge base is the *latest version id shared by both branches' histories*. Shared ids arise naturally from branching (copied history) and from prior merges (folded-in history), so sibling branches and repeated merges both get the correct base, like Git's merge-base.\n- **Structural merge** — `diffValues` builds a per-field delta tree of each side vs. base (objects recurse field-by-field; arrays and primitives are atomic values). `mergeDeltas` combines both delta trees: noop on either side takes the other, equal changes dedupe, otherwise a `Conflict` is recorded with dot-path, base/ours/theirs. The merged document is computed with conflicts resolved in favor of \"ours\".\n- **Application** — with zero conflicts the merge auto-applies: new documents carry their source history over, and when the source's versions linearly extend ours they fold in so `getHistory` reflects how content was reached; otherwise a single merge version is appended. Any conflict leaves the current branch untouched (`applied: false`).\n\n**Verification**\n- `npx vitest run` — 35/35 pass (disjoint-field merges, nested dot-path conflicts, add/remove-field merges, delete-vs-edit conflicts, sibling and repeated merges, no-op fast-forwards, deep-clone isolation, array atomicity)\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` — clean under `strict`\n- `npx eslint src/ tests/` — no findings\n\nOne behavior worth noting: `getHistory` throws for unknown documents but still returns the recorded history after a delete, which keeps `getVersion` usable for auditing removed documents — easy to change if you'd rather have deletion erase history access."}}
